---
import { GITHUB, ISSUES } from "../data";
import Section from "./Section.astro";
---

<Section id="faq" title="Questions">
  <div
    class="[&_details]:border-edge/60 [&_details]:border-b [&_p]:mt-0.5 [&_summary]:cursor-pointer [&_summary]:py-3 [&_summary]:font-semibold"
  >
    <details>
      <summary>Is it safe?</summary>
      <p>
        It reads a few files your addons already wrote in your game folder and sends them over HTTPS to the sites listed
        above, plus your Battle.net sign-in if you make one, the daily count and the update check. Its source is <a href={GITHUB}>public</a>, every line. The
        warning you see is about who signed the file, not about what's in it.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Does it touch the game?</summary>
      <p>
        No. It never runs inside the game, changes its files or reads its memory. It only reads the saved files World of
        Warcraft writes to disk when you log out or type /reload, the same files a backup tool would copy. Blizzard's
        rules are Blizzard's to state, and we don't speak for them.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Why isn't it signed?</summary>
      <p>
        A certificate Windows trusts costs money every year, and Ravenpost is one person's project. Until it's signed,
        the steps above get you past the warning, and the source is there to check.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What does it need?</summary>
      <p>
        On Windows 10 or 11, Microsoft Edge WebView2 for its window. It comes with Windows 11 and with an up-to-date
        Windows 10. On macOS, nothing beyond macOS 11. It's a small download because it uses your system's own web view
        instead of bundling a browser.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need it to use the addons?</summary>
      <p>
        No. Every addon works in the game without it. Ravenpost is only for reading Hearthtale's journal on your phone,
        seeing your characters on WoWLocker, or sharing what you see.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Does it keep running when I close it?</summary>
      <p>
        Yes, from the menu bar on macOS or the tray on Windows, so it can send your files at your next logout. Quit it
        from that icon. With "Open Ravenpost at login" on in its settings, it starts there quietly.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How do I remove it?</summary>
      <p>
        Quit it from the menu bar or the tray, then delete it: on macOS, drag Ravenpost from Applications to the Trash.
        On Windows, delete the .exe you downloaded. If you turned on "Open Ravenpost at login", turn it off first in
        Ravenpost's settings.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Something's wrong. Where do I tell you?</summary>
      <p>
        <a href={ISSUES}>Open an issue on GitHub</a>, with the Diagnostics text from Ravenpost's Settings if it starts.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>
</Section>
